{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778095784,"nonce":"nbsCOgViF9Jy5ab/gxjtjtXZ3f4=","title":"save_figure_with_spec: emit a reproducibility spec alongside each saved figure","message":"Per a recent rlrmp project-structure analysis, feedbax should emit a **figure spec** alongside each saved figure — a JSON-serializable record capturing everything needed to reproduce the figure from its sources, so reviewers can see what was generated without backing up every figure file.\n\n## Minimum viable feature\n\nAdd a `feedbax.plot.io.save_figure_with_spec(fig, spec, dst_dir)` helper (or similar) that mirrors feedbax's existing `_io.save()` \"PyTree-with-hyperparameters-header\" pattern, lifted to figures.\n\n**Spec contents** (proposed):\n- Input artifact paths + `sha256` of each.\n- Transform pipeline applied to the data (function names + kwargs).\n- Plot kwargs (axes, colors, markers).\n- Version pins: feedbax version, caller version (e.g. rlrmp), JAX version, key dep versions.\n- Random seeds (if applicable).\n- Timestamp + machine identifier (optional).\n\n**Output:** `dst_dir/\u003cfigure-name\u003e.json` (the spec) + optionally `dst_dir/\u003cfigure-name\u003e.\u003cext\u003e` (the figure file, threshold-gated for size).\n\n## Why this lives in feedbax (not the caller)\n\n- All feedbax downstream users hit the same problem.\n- The helper introspects feedbax plot signatures.\n- Mirrors the existing feedbax `_io.save` pattern.\n\n## Why now\n\nrlrmp is about to start filing analysis-specific issues (induced-gain analyser, Riccati teacher, etc.) that all produce figures. Without this helper, each analysis ad-hoc-pickles its plotting state, losing reproducibility. ~30 LOC in feedbax solves it once.\n\nA heavier decorator + replay system is **v2** and can wait until 20+ figures use v1.\n\n## References\n\n- `/tmp/project_structure_proposal.md` §5 (figure handling) — the rlrmp-side analysis that motivated this.\n- feedbax issue `488042f` (linearize protocol — separate but related: both are feedbax helpers extracted from rlrmp's analysis tooling).","files":null}]}